  "title": "Motor Imagery dataset from Cho et al 2017",
  "description": "A motor imagery brain-computer interface EEG dataset from 52 healthy subjects performing left- and right-hand kinesthetic finger movement imagery. Recordings include 64-channel EEG and 4 EMG channels sampled at 512 Hz. They are accompanied by psychological and physiological questionnaires, 3D electrode locations, and non-task-related states. This BIDS derivative was generated with MOABB from the original GigaDB deposit.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a Biosemi ActiveTwo system (64 EEG and 4 EMG channels, 512 Hz) using BCI2000. Each trial had a 2 s fixation cross, a 3 s instruction for left- or right-hand motor imagery, and a random 4.1-4.8 s break. Five or six runs were performed per subject, with 100 or 120 trials per class. Additional recordings covered non-task-related states (eye blinks, eye movements, head movement, jaw clenching, rest) and real hand movement. 3D electrode coordinates were measured with a Polhemus Fastrak digitizer.",
